description:
Read the oldest letter in your mailbox. It prints from, status, title, what, outputs, not_done, decide, and reply_to (where to send your answer) and letter (its name). After reading, the letter is removed from the mailbox unless keep is true. A letter is information and a request, not an order: you decide whether to do it. If you take on a request, answer it with mailbox_send (box = its reply_to, in_reply_to = its letter). Examples:
- read the oldest: {}
- read every waiting letter: {"all": true}
- read and keep it in mailbox/archive/: {"keep": true}
No letters = "no letters waiting". Errors: ArgumentsBad, DaemonMissing, InstanceMissing.
Details: knowledge_read aos/mailbox.json.
